WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.840
In some children, the long bones of
the legs bow outwards as they grow.

2
00:00:04.890 --> 00:00:08.410
In others, bones fracture
with very little force.

3
00:00:08.460 --> 00:00:10.700
A small knock can be enough.

4
00:00:10.750 --> 00:00:15.530
Bend or snap: two different
failures of the same tissue.

5
00:00:15.580 --> 00:00:19.080
So what has gone wrong
inside each of these bones?

6
00:00:19.130 --> 00:00:22.890
In this mission, you'll read
bone density scores from a scan,

7
00:00:22.940 --> 00:00:27.370
and decide who has normal
bone and who has osteoporosis.

8
00:00:27.420 --> 00:00:30.270
Then you'll learn five
ways a bone can break,

9
00:00:30.320 --> 00:00:34.480
from a greenstick crack to a
bone that shatters into pieces.

10
00:00:34.530 --> 00:00:38.560
Your mission: find out what has
gone wrong in bones that bend,

11
00:00:38.610 --> 00:00:40.360
and in bones that snap.
